---
import {
  API_CATALOG_PATH,
  API_CATALOG_PROFILE,
} from "../data/apiCatalog";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>API Discovery | The Valley Clean Team</title>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: light dark; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
      body { max-width: 48rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; }
      code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>API discovery</h1>
      <p>
        The Valley Clean Team publishes its public API catalog in the JSON
        Linkset format defined by RFC 9727.
      </p>
      <h2>Catalog endpoint</h2>
      <p><code>GET {API_CATALOG_PATH}</code></p>
      <p>
        Send <code>Accept: application/linkset+json</code>. A successful request
        returns <code>200 OK</code> and a <code>linkset</code> array. Each entry
        identifies an API with an <code>anchor</code> URL and related description
        and documentation links.
      </p>
      <p>
        <code>HEAD {API_CATALOG_PATH}</code> returns the same discovery headers
        without a response body.
      </p>
      <h2>Agent registration and provisioning</h2>
      <p><code>GET /agent/auth/register</code></p>
      <p>
        Returns the current anonymous-access and manual-email integration
        instructions as JSON. This read-only endpoint does not create an account
        or issue credentials. See <a href="/auth.md">auth.md</a> for the complete
        agent-facing policy.
      </p>
      <h2>Machine-readable description</h2>
      <p><a href="/openapi.json">OpenAPI 3.1 document</a></p>
      <p>
        Catalog profile: <a href={API_CATALOG_PROFILE}>{API_CATALOG_PROFILE}</a>
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
